### Orvexa API v1 — journey step 10: outbound messages
### Send a message (whatsapp | sms | email) — creates the outbound interaction
### and hands delivery to the provider; delivered/read receipts arrive as
### signed webhooks. NOTE: `from` is optional in api/openapi/orvexa-v1.yaml
### but this build requires source/destination endpoints — include `from`.

@ORVEXA_URL = {{$processEnv ORVEXA_URL}}
@ORVEXA_KEY = {{$processEnv ORVEXA_KEY}}

### Send an SMS → 201
# @name sendSms
POST {{ORVEXA_URL}}/api/v1/messages
X-API-Key: {{ORVEXA_KEY}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer_id": "{{createCustomer.response.body.$.data.id}}",
  "channel": "sms",
  "from": "orvexa-sms",
  "to": "+254712345678",
  "body": "Your ticket is resolved. Reply STOP to opt out."
}

###

### (Variant) WhatsApp send — same endpoint, channel=whatsapp, body ≤ 4096,
### media_urls optional array of strings:
# POST {{ORVEXA_URL}}/api/v1/messages
# X-API-Key: {{ORVEXA_KEY}}
# Content-Type: application/json
#
# {
#   "customer_id": "{{createCustomer.response.body.$.data.id}}",
#   "channel": "whatsapp",
#   "from": "orvexa-whatsapp",
#   "to": "+254712345678",
#   "body": "Your statement is ready."
# }
